  "strategy": "### Approach and Rationale\n\nThe primary idea is to employ a modified Bouncing Particle Optimization (BPO) strategy on a higher-resolution discretization to escape local optima and improve the overlap minimization. We increase the sample points (n_points) to 140, enhancing solution granularity, while using BPO's reflective boundaries to encourage exploration beyond conventional bounds. We leverage the initial_h_values as a warm start to expedite convergence, starting with a lower initial velocity for precision tuning. The higher population diversity and adaptive constraint handling aim to minimize the maximum overlap, targeting the Erdos constant bound.\n\n### Mathematical Specification\n\nWe represent h as a vector of n_points = 140 samples over [0, 2]. The variables are the sample values h[i]. The objective is:\n\n$$\n\\min_h \\max_k \\left( \\sum_{i=0}^{n_points-1} h[i](1 - h[(i+k) \\mod n_points]) \\right) \\times \\frac{2}{n_points}\n$$\n\nConstraints:\n1. 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n2. \u2211h[i] * (2.0 / n_points) = 1 \u21d2 \u2211h[i] = n_points / 2\n\n### Implementation Procedure\n\n1. **Initialization**\n   - Set n_points = 140, pop_size = 300, required_sum = n_points / 2\n   - Use initial_h_values as first particle, scaled to match required_sum\n   - Generate additional particles by perturbing initial_h_values within [0,1] and scaling\n\n2. **BPO Setup**\n   - Initialize velocities and positions\n   - Compute initial fitness for each particle\n\n3. **Optimization Loop**\n   - Update velocities and positions\n   - Reflect particles at boundaries using BPO rules\n   - Project to feasible region: clip h[i] to [0,1] and rescale to required_sum\n   - Update fitness and track best solutions\n\n4. **Termination**\n   - Stop after budget_s seconds or no improvement\n   - Return best feasible solution\n\n### Search Choices\n\n- **Velocity Bounds**: initial_velocity = 0.05, max_velocity = 0.2\n- **Inertia Weight**: 0.7, adjusted each iteration\n- **Population Diversity**: 300 particles for broader exploration\n\n### Compute Budget\n\n- **Per Iteration Cost**: approximates 0.1-0.2s with numpy optimizations\n- **Total Iterations**: ~5000 within 1100s budget\n- **Fallback**: Use initial_h_values if no improvement found\n\n### Validation\n\n- Ensure all h[i] \u2208 [0,1] and sum(h) = required_sum\n- Recompute C5 using evaluator to confirm results",
